    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i was looking at my student loan statement and the principal isnt going down as much as i thought it would even though i pay the same amount every month. can u explain how the interest actually works with the balance?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's the scoop: your payment is split between interest and principal, and the interest portion is calculated on your **current balance** each month — so early on, most of your payment goes to interest, not the balance. As the principal slowly shrinks, the interest charges shrink too, which means more of your same payment goes toward principal over time (this is called amortization). It's frustrating early on, but the back half of your loan pays down much faster.",
